---
// Rung 6 of the ladder, and the last: "What if your numbers are different?"
//
// This replaces a single <details> labelled "Show the workings and change the
// assumptions" which wrapped about 590 lines - the whole original page - and
// revealed all of it on one click. That is dd-002's origin case, and it was
// still standing at the bottom of the page the entry was written about: the
// ladder above it had been rebuilt and the cliff underneath had been left with
// a politer sign on it.
//
// Reviewed by Rahul and revised: the guardrails control is gone, the section
// headings are plain language instead of numbered jargon, the controls door
// opens by default, and the live answer sits above the doors - changing a
// number with no visible consequence is the worst kind of control.
//
// Two changes. It is framed as a RUNG, because after "what does protection
// cost?" the reader's honest next question is "but those are your numbers, not
// mine" - which turns a mystery door into a step. And the inside is split into
// three doors named by the question each answers, because layering by volume
// just moves the wall (dd-002); only layering by question is layering.
//
// Nothing is removed. dd-001 is satisfied by reachability, not by putting
// everything on screen at once.
//
// Slots: `controls`, `results`, `workings`.
---

<section id="rungExpert" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-4" aria-labelledby="rungExpertQ">
  <div class="card-premium rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">

    <div>
      <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.11em] text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
        Last question
      </p>
      <h2 id="rungExpertQ" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 mt-1">
        What if your numbers are different from ours?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 mt-2">
        Everything above was worked out from assumptions we chose — a rate of
        growth, a roughness, a tax rate, a horizon. None of them are facts. Here
        is every one of them, and everything the engine did with them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The answer, always visible, whichever door is open.
         Rahul, 15 Aug: "once the user changes the assumptions they dont see the
         result as the result is hidden in see it year by year." He is right and
         it was a fault of my own making - changing a number with no visible
         consequence is the worst kind of control. This is the ladder's own
         headline, live, in a fixed slot, using nothing the reader has not
         already been given. -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gold-500/30 bg-gold-500/5 px-4 py-3.5 space-y-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[0.11em] text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
        With your numbers
      </p>
      <p id="expertLiveHeadline" class="text-base font-semibold leading-snug text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">
        Working it out…
      </p>
      <p id="expertLiveDetail" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <!-- Open by default: the rung's question IS "change the assumptions", so
           the controls are the thing, not a door to the thing. -->
      <details open class="group rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 overflow-hidden">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-3.5 hover:bg-navy-50 dark:hover:bg-navy-900/60 transition-colors focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-gold-500/50">
          <span>
            <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Change the assumptions</span>
            <span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">savings, income, growth, roughness, tax, horizon, protection</span>
          </span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 text-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 p-4 sm:p-5">
          <slot name="controls" />
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 overflow-hidden">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-3.5 hover:bg-navy-50 dark:hover:bg-navy-900/60 transition-colors focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-gold-500/50">
          <span>
            <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">See it year by year</span>
            <span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">the full projection, the paycheck schedule and the range of outcomes</span>
          </span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 text-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 p-4 sm:p-5">
          <slot name="results" />
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 overflow-hidden">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-3.5 hover:bg-navy-50 dark:hover:bg-navy-900/60 transition-colors focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-gold-500/50">
          <span>
            <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Check the workings</span>
            <span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">what the protection cost, year by year, and what the floor absorbed</span>
          </span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 text-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 p-4 sm:p-5">
          <slot name="workings" />
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // One subscriber to the shared result (dd-013). No computation here.
  window.addEventListener('swp:result', (e) => {
    const d = (e as CustomEvent).detail;
    const o = d?.outlook;
    if (!o) return;
    const head = document.getElementById('expertLiveHeadline');
    const detail = document.getElementById('expertLiveDetail');
    if (!head || !detail) return;

    const years = d.inputs.horizonYears;
    const lasted = Math.round(o.survival * 100);
    head.textContent =
      o.medianDepletionYear !== null
        ? `Your money typically runs out in year ${o.medianDepletionYear} of ${years}.`
        : `Your money lasts the full ${years} years.`;
    detail.textContent =
      `It lasted in ${lasted} of every 100 futures. Change anything below and this line moves.`;
  });
</script>
